Ladybird ends the percentage height calculation quirk’s search at a
button, as one that lays out its content as a flex container. Chrome
keeps such a button at its min-height, as the issue’s screenshots show.

WebKit lays out a button as a flexbox (its RenderButton is a
RenderFlexibleBox), so the quirk never walks through one. And Gecko’s
IsQuirkContainingBlockHeight, in layout/generic/ReflowInput.cpp,
continues the walk only through block and scroll-container frames,
which a button frame isn’t.
